# Local scratch that must never be committed (noetl/ai-meta housekeeping).
#
# Two accidental `git add -A` runs in one session staged ~11k files from these
# paths.  The repo root carries a large untracked surface — a Python venv, git
# worktrees, MCP browser traces — so `git add -A` is never the right command
# here.  Ignoring them removes the trap rather than relying on remembering.
#
# `.worktrees/` in particular holds full checkouts of every submodule branch
# under active work; committing it would inline whole repos into ai-meta.
.slm-venv/
.slm_logs/
.slm_registry/
.worktrees/
.playwright-mcp/
